        {
          "id": "ch_msgs92h93u7m",
          "title": "Counting Teeth: Gear Ratios",
          "summary": "Learners build the core ratio equation from tooth counts and see idlers cancel.",
          "sections": [
            {
              "id": "sec_msgs92h9frdr",
              "title": "The Ratio Rule",
              "type": "h5",
              "summary": "Step 1.2 tooth counting and Ratio = Driven/Driver = 40/10 = 4:1 figure.",
              "purpose": "Student marks a tooth on each gear, turns the driver, counts driven turns, and derives driven/driver.",
              "vr": {},
              "reading": {
                "chunks": []
              },
              "h5": {
                "prompt": "Build an interactive two-gear tooth-counting bench that makes the student CONSTRUCT the insight 'gear ratio = driven teeth / driver teeth, found by counting teeth — not by eyeballing size.'\n\nLAYOUT: Two meshed spur gears drawn on a 2D canvas. The DRIVER gear (left, labeled 'Driver / input') is visibly SMALL but the student can toggle its rendered radius; the DRIVEN gear (right, labeled 'Driven / output') is visibly LARGE. Each gear has a bright taped tooth marker (a colored notch). Above the canvas: two number readouts — 'Driver teeth' and 'Driven teeth'.\n\nSTEP 1 — PREDICT (defeat misconception first): Present a preset where the driven gear LOOKS about 4x bigger than the driver. Ask the student to guess, WITHOUT counting: 'If you turn the driver 1 full turn, how many turns does the driven gear make?' Provide a slider/entry for their guess. Log it — do not correct yet.\n\nSTEP 2 — COUNT: Add a 'Count teeth' mode. Clicking each gear highlights teeth one-by-one and increments a counter, forcing the student to arrive at exact counts (e.g. driver = 10, driven = 40). Show the two counts.\n\nSTEP 3 — MANIPULATE: A 'Turn driver +1 rotation' button rotates the driver a full turn; the driven gear rotates the meshed amount and its taped marker returns to start only after driver/driven = teeth ratio worth of driver turns. A rotation tally shows: driver turns vs driven turns. Student sees the driven gear makes only 1/4 turn per driver turn (or the reciprocal, depending on which is driver) — the physical outcome.\n\nSTEP 4 — REVEAL: Show the formula filling in: Ratio = Driven / Driver = 40 / 10 = 4:1, and a verdict badge 'Driven turns SLOWER (4x)'. Compare this exact computed result against the student's Step-1 eyeball guess with a message like 'Counting gives the real answer — size by eye can mislead.'\n\nEXPLORE: Let the student change tooth counts via +/- controls (driver 5–40, driven 5–40, independent of drawn size to break the size=ratio assumption; optionally let a small-drawn gear have MORE teeth). On every change, recompute ratio and update the SLOWER/FASTER verdict live (driven faster if driven<driver teeth). Give feedback text confirming increase vs decrease.\n\nDATA/PRESETS: 10/40 (4:1 slower), 40/10 (1:4 faster), 12/24 (2:1 slower), plus a trap preset where the physically bigger-drawn gear actually has FEWER teeth so eyeballing fails.\n\nColors and gear teeth drawn simply in 2D; no external assets. Reflect the source figure: Ratio = Driven/Driver = 40/10 = 4:1.",
                "html": "<div style=\"max-width:820px;margin:auto;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#1a2233;padding:10px\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align:center\">The Ratio Rule — Tooth-Counting Bench</h2>\n\n<div style=\"background:#eef4ff;border:1px solid #b8ccf0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;margin-bottom:10px\">\n<b>Step 1 — Predict (no counting!):</b> The driven gear on the right <i>looks</i> about 4× bigger.\nIf you turn the driver <b>1</b> full turn, how many turns does the driven gear make?\n<div style=\"margin-top:6px\">Your guess:\n<input id=\"guess\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" style=\"width:70px\" value=\"1\">\n<button onclick=\"logGuess()\" style=\"cursor:pointer\">Lock guess</button>\n<span id=\"guessMsg\" style=\"margin-left:8px;color:#555\"></span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;margin-bottom:6px\">\n<span>Driver teeth: <span id=\"dtDisp\">?</span></span>\n<span>Driven teeth: <span id=\"vtDisp\">?</span></span>\n</div>\n\n<canvas id=\"cv\" width=\"800\" height=\"360\" style=\"border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:8px;width:100%;background:#fafcff\"></canvas>\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;margin:8px 0\">\n<button id=\"countBtn\" onclick=\"toggleCount()\" style=\"cursor:pointer\">Enter Count-teeth mode</button>\n<button onclick=\"turnDriver()\" style=\"cursor:pointer\">Turn driver +1 rotation</button>\n<button onclick=\"reset()\" style=\"cursor:pointer\">Reset markers</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"tally\" style=\"text-align:center;color:#333\"></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;margin:10px 0\">\n<b>Presets:</b>\n<button onclick=\"preset(10,40)\">10 / 40</button>\n<button onclick=\"preset(40,10)\">40 / 10</button>\n<button onclick=\"preset(12,24)\">12 / 24</button>\n<button onclick=\"preset(8,32,true)\">Trap</button>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;margin:8px 0\">\nDriver teeth: <button onclick=\"chg('d',-1)\">−</button> <span id=\"dNum\"></span> <button onclick=\"chg('d',1)\">+</button>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;\nDriven teeth: <button onclick=\"chg('v',-1)\">−</button> <span id=\"vNum\"></span> <button onclick=\"chg('v',1)\">+</button>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"reveal\" style=\"background:#fff7e6;border:1px solid #f0d68c;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;text-align:center;font-size:15px\"></div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:10px\">\n<img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"max-width:100%;border-radius:8px\" alt=\"compound gear train\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666\">Real compound gear train — ratio still = driven ÷ driver teeth.</div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\nvar driverTeeth=10, drivenTeeth=40;\nvar driverAngle=0, drivenAngle=0;\nvar driverTurns=0, drivenTurns=0;\nvar countMode=false, counted={d:0,v:0}, guessLocked=null, trap=false;\nvar cv=document.getElementById('cv'), ctx=cv.getContext('2d');\n\nfunction logGuess(){\n  guessLocked=parseFloat(document.getElementById('guess').value);\n  document.getElementById('guessMsg').textContent=\"Guess locked: \"+guessLocked+\" turn(s). Now count!\";\n}\nfunction toggleCount(){\n  countMode=!countMode;\n  document.getElementById('countBtn').textContent=countMode?\"Exit Count mode\":\"Enter Count-teeth mode\";\n  draw();\n}\nfunction reset(){driverAngle=0;drivenAngle=0;driverTurns=0;drivenTurns=0;updateTally();draw();}\nfunction preset(d,v,t){driverTeeth=d;drivenTeeth=v;trap=!!t;counted={d:0,v:0};reset();update();}\nfunction chg(g,n){\n  if(g=='d'){driverTeeth=Math.max(5,Math.min(40,driverTeeth+n));}\n  else{drivenTeeth=Math.max(5,Math.min(40,drivenTeeth+n));}\n  update();reset();\n}\nfunction update(){\n  document.getElementById('dNum').textContent=driverTeeth;\n  document.getElementById('vNum').textContent=drivenTeeth;\n  var shownD=countMode||counted.d?counted.d:driverTeeth;\n  document.getElementById('dtDisp').textContent=counted.d?counted.d:driverTeeth;\n  document.getElementById('vtDisp').textContent=counted.v?counted.v:drivenTeeth;\n  computeReveal();\n  draw();\n}\nfunction turnDriver(){\n  driverTurns++;\n  driverAngle+=Math.PI*2;\n  // meshed: driven rotates driverTeeth/drivenTeeth of a turn\n  drivenAngle-=Math.PI*2*(driverTeeth/drivenTeeth);\n  drivenTurns=driverTurns*(driverTeeth/drivenTeeth);\n  updateTally();\n  animateTo();\n}\nfunction updateTally(){\n  document.getElementById('tally').innerHTML=\n    \"Driver turns: <b>\"+driverTurns+\"</b> &nbsp; Driven turns: <b>\"+drivenTurns.toFixed(2)+\"</b>\";\n}\nfunction computeReveal(){\n  var ratio=(drivenTeeth/driverTeeth);\n  var faster=drivenTeeth<driverTeeth;\n  var rStr;\n  if(faster) rStr=\"1 : \"+(driverTeeth/drivenTeeth).toFixed(2).replace(/\\.00$/,'');\n  else rStr=(drivenTeeth/driverTeeth).toFixed(2).replace(/\\.00$/,'')+\" : 1\";\n  var verdict=faster?\n    \"Driven turns <b style='color:#c0392b'>FASTER (\"+(driverTeeth/drivenTeeth).toFixed(2)+\"×)</b> — speed increase\":\n    \"Driven turns <b style='color:#1e6fa8'>SLOWER (\"+ratio.toFixed(2)+\"×)</b> — speed decrease\";\n  var guessCmp=\"\";\n  if(guessLocked!==null){\n    var real=driverTeeth/drivenTeeth; // driven turns per 1 driver turn\n    guessCmp=\"<hr>Your eyeball guess: <b>\"+guessLocked+\"</b> turn(s). Real answer: <b>\"+real.toFixed(3)+\"</b> turn(s) of the driven per 1 driver turn.<br><i>Counting gives the real answer — size by eye can mislead\"+(trap?\", especially in the Trap preset!\":\"\")+\"</i>\";\n  }\n  document.getElementById('reveal').innerHTML=\n    \"<b>Step 4 — Reveal</b><br>Ratio = Driven ÷ Driver = \"+drivenTeeth+\" / \"+driverTeeth+\" = <b>\"+rStr+\"</b><br>\"+verdict+guessCmp;\n}\n\n// canvas gear geometry: driver small drawn, driven large drawn\nfunction gearGeom(){\n  return {\n    dx:230, dy:180, dr: trap?60:55,           // driver drawn radius\n    vx:560, vy:180, vr: trap?55:120           // driven drawn radius (trap: smaller though more teeth)\n  };\n}\nfunction drawGear(cx,cy,r,teeth,angle,color,mk){\n  ctx.save();ctx.translate(cx,cy);ctx.rotate(angle);\n  ctx.beginPath();\n  for(var i=0;i<teeth;i++){\n    var a=i/teeth*Math.PI*2;\n    var ro=r, ri=r-9;\n    ctx.lineTo(Math.cos(a)*ri,Math.sin(a)*ri);\n    ctx.lineTo(Math.cos(a+0.12)*ro,Math.sin(a+0.12)*ro);\n    ctx.lineTo(Math.cos(a+ (Math.PI/teeth)-0.12)*ro,Math.sin(a+(Math.PI/teeth)-0.12)*ro);\n    ctx.lineTo(Math.cos(a+Math.PI/teeth)*ri,Math.sin(a+Math.PI/teeth)*ri);\n  }\n  ctx.closePath();ctx.fillStyle=color;ctx.fill();ctx.strokeStyle=\"#333\";ctx.stroke();\n  ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(0,0,r*0.25,0,7);ctx.fillStyle=\"#fff\";ctx.fill();ctx.stroke();\n  // marker notch at tooth 0\n  ctx.save();ctx.rotate(0);\n  ctx.beginPath();ctx.rect(r-14,-4,16,8);ctx.fillStyle=mk;ctx.fill();ctx.stroke();\n  ctx.restore();\n  ctx.restore();\n}\nvar hoverInfo=null;\nfunction draw(){\n  ctx.clearRect(0,0,800,360);\n  var g=gearGeom();\n  drawGear(g.dx,g.dy,g.dr,driverTeeth,driverAngle,\"#5b8def\",\"#ff4136\");\n  drawGear(g.vx,g.vy,g.vr,drivenTeeth,drivenAngle,\"#2ecc71\",\"#ff851b\");\n  ctx.fillStyle=\"#1a2233\";ctx.font=\"14px Arial\";ctx.textAlign=\"center\";\n  ctx.fillText(\"Driver / input\",g.dx,g.dy+g.dr+22);\n  ctx.fillText(\"Driven / output\",g.vx,g.vy+g.vr+22);\n  if(countMode){\n    ctx.fillStyle=\"#c0392b\";ctx.font=\"13px Arial\";\n    ctx.fillText(\"Count mode: click a gear to tally its teeth (\"+counted.d+\" / \"+counted.v+\")\",400,30);\n  }\n}\ncv.addEventListener('click',function(e){\n  if(!countMode)return;\n  var r=cv.getBoundingClientRect();\n  var x=(e.clientX-r.left)*(800/r.width), y=(e.clientY-r.top)*(360/r.height);\n  var g=gearGeom();\n  if(Math.hypot(x-g.dx,y-g.dy)<g.dr+10){\n    if(counted.d<driverTeeth){counted.d++;driverAngle+=0.03;}\n    if(counted.d>=driverTeeth){/*done*/}\n  } else if(Math.hypot(x-g.vx,y-g.vy)<g.vr+10){\n    if(counted.v<drivenTeeth){counted.v++;drivenAngle+=0.02;}\n  }\n  update();\n});\n\nvar animT=null;\nfunction animateTo(){draw();}\n\npreset(10,40);\n</script>\n</div>",
                "status": "ready",
                "followUp": {
                  "enabled": true,
                  "type": "short",
                  "question": "A driver gear with 8 teeth meshes with a driven gear that has 24 teeth. What is the gear ratio, and does the driven gear turn faster or slower?",
                  "options": [
                    "",
                    "",
                    "",
                    ""
                  ],
                  "answer": "3:1, and the driven gear turns slower (one-third the speed).",
                  "explanation": "Ratio = driven teeth / driver teeth = 24/8 = 3:1. Because the driven gear has more teeth than the driver, it turns once for every 3 driver turns — so it turns 3 times slower. You get this from counting teeth, not from how big the gears look."
                }
              },
